<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stanisław of Masovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1501">1501</a>–<a href="/years/1524">1524</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stanisław of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> (1501–1524) was one of the last Piast dukes of Masovia, ruling jointly with his brother Janusz III, at first under the regency of their mother, Anna Radziwiłł. He died young and without heirs in 1524, and after Janusz III's death in 1526 Masovia was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stanislaw-of-masovia.jpg" alt="Stanisław of Masovia" width="232" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Masovia)Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stanis%C5%82aw_Mazowiecki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
